+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+A client MAY request its conversation summaries over the authenticated socket by sending `list_conversations`. When `transport.history.enabled` is true, the server answers with `conversation_list`, containing only summaries owned by the authenticated connection user; a `userId` supplied in the frame does not change whose conversations are returned. Summary timestamps are ISO strings ([validated by: answers an authenticated client with only its own conversation summaries](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L8)).
+
